      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "50 patients admitted for lumbago or sciatica are examined for their \"static\". Radiographs of the lumbar-pelvis-hip-joint region are taken in 2 planes with the patient standing. An oblique pelvis is a certain, a reduced angle of Leger a probable influence of lumbosciatic pain. The high-assimilation-pelvis of Gutmann produces an unfavorable prognosis."},
